{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1483 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "1c28568ae2b534fa24e9468289da0d797e5aecd3f98e329a5ee602f7240f00fa" :edb/db-before-t 1482 :edb/db-after-t 1483 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534795 50 #inst "2026-10-08T07:07:18.229Z" 13194139534795 true] [17592186059679 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310549 13194139534795 true] [17592186059679 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310557 13194139534795 true] [17592186059680 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310564 13194139534795 true] [17592186059680 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310567 13194139534795 true] [17592186059680 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310572 13194139534795 true] [17592186059681 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310542 13194139534795 true] [17592186060075 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534795 true] [17592186060075 1100 "Determine the entry $a_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139534795 false] [17592186060075 1100 "Determine the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534795 true] [17592186060075 1145 "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|-(-2)|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+4|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(6-0)+2(0+1)+4(0+3) \\\\  & =6+2+12 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(-4-0) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21}=\\frac{1}{20}\\cdot 4=\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534795 true] [17592186283608 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310571 13194139534795 true] [17592186310542 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310543 13194139534795 true] [17592186310542 1089 "q-104413" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310542 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534795 true] [17592186310542 1100 "Determine the entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A$ $=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310542 1113 #uuid "b2dc099c-b9ae-5747-a320-990b6201e0cb" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310542 1145 "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}A=|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(1-0)-0+(-1-0) \\\\  & =3+0-1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{32}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{32} & =(-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(0-1) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{23}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{32}=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310543 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310544 13194139534795 true] [17592186310543 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310545 13194139534795 true] [17592186310543 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310546 13194139534795 true] [17592186310543 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310547 13194139534795 true] [17592186310543 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310548 13194139534795 true] [17592186310543 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534795 true] [17592186310543