2186310549 1145 "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-17 & -12 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-17 & 12 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-17 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 12 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-17 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 12 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310550 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310551 13194139534795 true] [17592186310550 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310552 13194139534795 true] [17592186310550 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534795 true] [17592186310550 1041 "field-1" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310550 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310552 13194139534795 true] [17592186310550 1110 #uuid "52bf03b0-9bac-5c2f-a9fd-8c90c57bebf4" 13194139534795 