- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{7}\\,\\,$ |  | $-11$ | {{field-2}} | $3$ |  |\n|  |  | $-4$ | {{field-3}} | $3$ |  |" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310557 1113 #uuid "70daf951-b8fd-5de4-97d2-057221cebad2" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310557 1145 "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 11 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -10 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -11 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -10 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -11 & -10 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -11 & -10 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310558 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310559 13194139534795 true] [17592186310558 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534795 true] [17592186310558 1041 "field-1" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310558 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310559 13194139534795 true] [17592186310558 1110 #uuid "b8cd9a5f-5e9e-5780-86cc-fdfe1d030772" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310559 1034 "1" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310559 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534795 true] [17592186310559 1111 #uuid "e267c69c-11b0-56c9-8a03-72cacb05bb71" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310560 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310561 13194139534795 true] [17592186310560 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534795 true] [17592186310560 1041 "field-2" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310560 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310561 13194139534795 true] [17592186310560 1110 #uuid "b12a7aba-a704-53eb-a3bb-01a5a157d455" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310561 1034 "-10" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310561 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534795 true] [17592186310561 1111 #uuid "3e87af07-bd78-5b6b-9782-ab45832e8cdd" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310562 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310563 13194139534795 true] [17592186310562 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534795 true] [17592186310562 1041 "field-3" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310562 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310563 13194139534795 true] [17592186310562 1110 #uuid "9e2b76ac-ebcf-5052-aa8a-690728e00b35" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310563 1034 "-3" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310563 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534795 true] [17592186310563 1111 #uuid "e1628abe-17c7-5e2a-b8c7-5edc553bd2e0" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310564 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310565 13194139534795 true] [17592186310564 1089 "q-319434" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310564 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534795 true] [17592186310564 1100 "The entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & k\\end{aligned}]$\nequals $\\frac{1}{3}$ and $det(A)=1-2k.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310564 1113 #uuid "27633a9f-8981-5e23-907e-da217010fa96" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310564 1145 "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=1-2k\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}^{t}={c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(1\\cdot k-0\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =-k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(1-2k)}\\cdot (-k) \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{\\,2k-1\\,}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{12}^{′}=\\frac{1}{3}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k}{\\,2k-1\\,} & =\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 3k & =2k-1 \\\\ k & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310565 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310566 13194139534795 true] [17592186310565 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534795 true] [17592186310565 1041 "field-1" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310565 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310566 13194139534795 true] [17592186310565 1110 #uuid "f4964ddd-44a7-5cc3-a80f-e165279c2020" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310566 1034 "-1" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310566 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534795 true] [17592186310566 1111 #uuid "4933487e-ae48-5963-ac90-702135f7876e" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310567 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310568 13194139534795 true] [17592186310567 1089 "q-319859" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310567 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534795 true] [17592186310567 1100 "The entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ k & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nequals $-\\frac{1}{2}.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310567 1113 #uuid "4685104e-5c8e-5535-9bd4-12467257f628" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310567 1145 "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ k & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ k & 2\\end{aligned}|+(-1)|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ k & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\,(1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-1))-2\\,(0\\cdot 2-1\\cdot k)+(-1)\\,(0\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot k) \\\\  & =(2+1)-2\\,(-k)+(-1)\\,(-k) \\\\  & =3+2k+k \\\\  & =3k+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need ${c}_{12}^{t}={c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(2\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =-(4-1) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3k+3}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{3k+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we are told that ${a}_{12}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{2}$, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-3}{3k+3} & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -3k-3 & =-6 \\\\ -3k & =-6+3 \\\\ k & =\\frac{-3}{-3} \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310568 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310569 13194139534795 true] [17592186310568 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310570 13194139534795 true] [17592186310568 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534795 true] [17592186310568 1041 "field-1" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310568 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310569 13194139534795 true] [17592186310568 1110 #uuid "b6b25f54-747f-5260-9908-969b50f76fbf" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310569 1034 "1" 13194139534795 true] [17592186310569 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534795 true] [17592186310569 1111 #uuid "604e9b23-51c3-5262-b35b-